    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d30">

                <pb facs="0105" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v17p1/pg70"/>

                <head>30. Memorandum from the Vice President’s Assistant for National Security
                    Affairs (Clift) to Vice President
                        Mondale<anchor n="1" xml:id="d30-f1"
                    />
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <idno type="document-identifier">Memo No. 1526–77</idno>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1977-09-27">September 27, 1977</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Meeting with President of Djibouti—Additional Background</item>
                </list>
                <p>The State Department has forwarded a draft report on President Hassan Gouled’s meeting with Warren Christopher yesterday (Tab A) together
                    with additional suggestions for talking points (Tab B).<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d30-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>—If President Gouled brings up his request
                    for additional aid, you should say it will receive the most careful attention,
                    that you know we have experts at work on the problem and that you are aware that
                    the subject was raised with Mr. Christopher. Dick Moose
                    can expand on this during the meeting.</p>



                <xi:include href="d30-a1.xml" xpointer="d30-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d30-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d30-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, Papers of Walter F.
                        Mondale, Box 42, Foreign Countries—Africa, 7–12/77 [2].
                    Confidential. Sent for information.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d30-f2" n="2" xml:id="d30-f2-content">
                <p>Tab B is attached but not printed. See <ref target="#d33">Document 33</ref> for
                        Mondale’s meeting with President
                        Gouled. In telegram 235953 to
                    Djibouti, October 1, the Department reported on Gouled’s talks with other U.S. officials. (National Archives, RG
                    59, Central Foreign Policy File, D770357–1040)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
